    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-13845",
      "knowledge_point_id": "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating Definite Integrals",
      "problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $e/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
