      "knowledge_point_id": "e803bd99-388f-5146-ab91-03fd7b658c2c",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Products Containing the Exponential Function",
      "problem": "$\\int 6{x}^{2}{e}^{5-2{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=5-2{x}^{3}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=6{x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}{e}^{5-2{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{5-2{x}^{3}}\\cdot 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot \\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =-{e}^{5-2{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
